WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.658
UV light can cause adjacent cytosines and thymines to form

00:00:04.658 --> 00:00:09.688
covalent bonds. The resulting distortion in the DNA backbone interferes

00:00:09.688 --> 00:00:12.638
with normal copying and transcription.

00:00:12.638 --> 00:00:16.002
This is damage that must be recognized and removed.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:20.247
Repair proteins recognize the damaged site.

00:00:20.247 --> 00:00:23.645
Enzymes cut the backbone on either side of the problem

00:00:23.645 --> 00:00:27.073
and remove the damaged section from that strand.

00:00:27.073 --> 00:00:30.083
The diagram shows the gap left by that removal.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.400
The missing section is replaced with correct DNA nucleotides.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.776
The backbone is then resealed by forming phosphodiester linkages.

00:00:39.776 --> 00:00:41.448
Remember the sequence:

00:00:41.448 --> 00:00:44.634
recognize the damage, cut out the section,

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:47.070
replace it, and reseal the backbone.
